{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "וירא העם וינועו", :translit "vayar ha-am vayanu'u", :gloss "and the people saw and they trembled"} {:he "על כן מתנענעים בשעת לימוד התורה", :translit "al ken mitna'na'im b'sha'at limud ha-torah", :gloss "therefore one sways at the time of Torah study"} {:he "לפי שהתורה ניתנה באימה ברתת ובזיע", :translit "lfi sheha-torah nitnah b'imah b'ratet uv'zi'a", :gloss "because the Torah was given in awe, in trembling, and in sweating"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Practice of swaying during Torah study linked to the conditions of Sinai."}], :frame {:text "The Torah was given at Sinai in a state of awe, trembling, and fear, as the verse states (Exodus 20:15) 'And all the people saw the thunderings.' The description of the giving of the Torah as accompanied by trembling and sweating appears in the Talmud, and the practice of swaying during Torah study is presented as a continuation of that awe.", :sources ["Shabbat 88a" "Exodus 20:15"]}} {:quotes [{:he "וינועו", :translit "vayanu'u", :gloss "and they trembled"} {:he "י\"ב מילין", :translit "yud-bet milin", :gloss "twelve milin (miles)"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "וינועו", :b "י\"ב מילין"}], :frame {:text "When the Torah was given at Sinai, Israel recoiled twelve mil in fear at each utterance, and ministering angels had to assist them back, as recorded in the Talmud. The Ba'al HaTurim encodes the distance of their recoil in the gematria of the word 'וינועו.'", :sources ["Shabbat 88b"]}} {:quotes [{:he "וינועו", :translit "vayanu'u", :gloss "and they trembled"} {:he "וינועו אמות הספים מקול הקורא", :translit "vayanu'u amot ha-sapim mi-kol ha-korei", :gloss "and the doorposts of the thresholds trembled from the voice of the caller"} {:he "מלכי צבאות ידודון ידודון", :translit "malchei tzeva'ot yiddodon yiddodon", :gloss "kings of hosts will flee, will flee"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["וינועו" "וינועו אמות הספים"]} {:kind :other, :note "Gezera shava between the two occurrences: trembling caused by angels in both."}], :frame {:text "The phrase 'וינועו אמות הספים מקול הקורא' appears in Isaiah 6:4, where the doorposts shook at the voice of the seraph calling to Isaiah. The verse 'מלכי צבאות ידודון ידודון' appears in Psalms 68:13. By linking the two occurrences of 'וינועו' through a gezera shava, the Ba'al HaTurim draws a parallel: just as the trembling in Isaiah's vision was caused by an angel, so too the trembling at Sinai was caused by angels.", :sources ["Isaiah 6:4" "Psalms 68:13"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Practice of swaying during Torah study linked to the conditions of Sinai.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "וינועו", :a-value 148, :b "י\"ב מילין", :b-value 152, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["וינועו" "וינועו אמות הספים"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "וינועו", :refs ["Psalms 107:27"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "וינועו אמות הספים", :refs ["Isaiah 6:4"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive}]} {:kind :other, :note "Gezera shava between the two occurrences: trembling caused by angels in both.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:17:47.107976933Z", :model "glm-5.2"}